📚 Theory Notes
1. What is Python?
High-level programming language.
Easy to read and write.
Interpreted language.
Dynamically typed.
Popular for AI, Automation, Web Development and Data Science.
2. Variables

A variable is a named memory location used to store data.

Java
String city = "Goa";
Python
city = "Goa"

Python automatically determines the variable type.

3. Dynamic Typing

Python determines the data type at runtime.

Example

x = 10
x = "Hello"

Both statements are valid.

Unlike Java, variables can store different data types at different times.

4. Data Types
Data Type	Example
int	10
float	10.5
str	"Hello"
bool	True / False
5. Printing Output
print("Hello")

Using f-string

name = "Tushar"

print(f"My name is {name}")

Use f-strings whenever variables need to be displayed inside text.

